* A module contains sensitive configuration values that should not be accessible directly by other modules. How would you design the module?
* A Node.js application has hundreds of modules and startup time is increasing. How would you investigate module loading and initialization?
* A production application shows stale configuration values after configuration files are changed. How could module caching be responsible?
* Two modules depend on each other and one receives incomplete data during startup. How would you diagnose and resolve the circular dependency?
* A team is migrating a CommonJS application to ES Modules. What migration issues would you expect?
* A package works correctly with `require()` but fails when imported using `import`. How would you investigate the interoperability issue?
* A Node.js project has both `.js` and `.mjs` files and developers are confused about how they are interpreted. How would you standardize the module strategy?
* A project changes `"type": "commonjs"` to `"type": "module"` and many files start failing. What areas would you inspect?
* A service needs to load different payment-provider implementations based on configuration. How would you design a dynamic module/plugin architecture?
* An application supports multiple database implementations such as MySQL and PostgreSQL. How would you use modules to keep the business logic independent of the database?
* A unit test is difficult to write because a service directly imports and creates its dependencies. How would you redesign the modules for better testability?
* A shared utility module maintains mutable global state, and different requests affect each other. How would you redesign it?
